{"availability":"available","full":"rvyyv-n/bookcook","name":"bookcook","description":"a cookbook you can talk to","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-28T20:32:11Z","updated":"2026-09-30T13:08:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bookcook.pages.dev","topics":["cookbook","cookbook-app","cross-platform","recipes","recipes-app","webapp"],"demo":"https://bookcook.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.395Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.395Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.395Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.395Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Save the recipes that only live in someone's head by saying them out loud,","Bookcook is for the family cook who wears reading glasses and has busy hands: very large text, big targets, and voice for everything. Tell it a recipe the way you'd tell a friend, and it turns what you said into ingredients, steps and timers, keeping the story behind the dish in the teller's own voice."],"features":["Tell it. A gentle interview, one question at a time: the name, whose recipe it is, how many it feeds, the ingredients, the steps, tips and the story behind it. Ingredients appear as you say them and durations become…","Just talk. Talk while you cook; Bookcook sorts it into ingredients and steps for you to check, and keeps every word as \"In her words\".","Type it, paste it or bring a link. Type the way you'd say it (2 cups basmati rice, washed) with a live preview, paste messy text from WhatsApp or notes and have it tidied up, or import a recipe website's page.","Check before saving. Whichever way it came in, you check it on one screen, with anything the parser was unsure of marked. Drafts save as you go, and every text field has a Speak button.","Cook mode. One step at a time, in type you can read from across the kitchen. Steps are read aloud, voice commands (next, back, repeat, timer, stop) move you along without touching the screen, and the screen stays awake."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rvyyv-n/bookcook/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3b9157965f31be2eb4bc556e6c1cb43633ae81a155ae689b92483043166572b4","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.480Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.480Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Save the recipes that only live in someone's head by saying them out loud,","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rvyyv-n/bookcook/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"There's no account, no server holding your data and no analytics.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rvyyv-n/bookcook/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"3b9157965f31be2eb4bc556e6c1cb43633ae81a155ae689b92483043166572b4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rvyyv-n/bookcook/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.480Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-30T13:08:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rvyyv-n/bookcook/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T19:07:16.482Z","hash":"3b9157965f31be2eb4bc556e6c1cb43633ae81a155ae689b92483043166572b4","originalBytes":18528,"storedBytes":18528,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["app","run","npm","design","recipe","bookcook","install","docs","voice","android","one","open","windows","every","screen","text","build","cook","link","parser","when","back","browser","github","ingredients","them","website","what","add","built","check","cookbook","dev","function","it.","new","only","own","pages","recipes","runs","speech","src","tap","they","version","works","chrome","cloudflare","download","edge","file","first","icons","live","release","releases","share","tell","there","type","apk","builds","checks","license","notes","react","say","see","server","settings","site","talk","aloud","behind","bookcook.pages.dev","deploy","desktop","features","home","how","icon",